# What NOT to upload to Vercel.
#
# The CLI does not honour .gitignore, so without this it would push
# node_modules, the client's source material (PDF + raw extractions) and the
# local screenshot archive. Vercel installs dependencies and runs the build
# itself.
#
# EVERY PATTERN IS ANCHORED WITH A LEADING SLASH. Without it a pattern matches
# at any depth: a bare `scripts` would also exclude src/scripts/, which strips
# the client modules and fails the build with
#   [UNRESOLVED_IMPORT] Could not resolve '../scripts/app.client'

/node_modules
/dist
/.astro
/.git

# Local-only working material, never part of the deployed site.
/ressources
/screenshots
/scripts

.env
.env.*
.DS_Store
